{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-set-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0057","math_ordinal":201,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof has just defined H as the union of the disjoint integration intervals and established its measure bound; F is undefined in this argument, so the final integral must be over H.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt225.tex:286","source_normalized_sha256":"459c55c5e103b02e894d27d4a5822033887e7d23f53c600f6e0718b8b1296aa2","source_text":"$\\int_F|f|\\le\\epsilon$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt225.tex:284","target_normalized_sha256":"f5cc2d7fcf6a07da74c2ecc5f683414b496cbb6c4fb63bfce4a9ff99189a2ba3","target_text":"$\\int_H|f|\\le\\epsilon$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S225"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-order-relation","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0058","math_ordinal":252,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The ordered interval-endpoint chain requires an order relation between b_1 and the continuation; inserting the missing less-than-or-equal sign restores the same hypothesis used throughout the section.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt225.tex:355","source_normalized_sha256":"f98c1b85c9cbccc3c4cfca781cef0ff40b303e4194fac9a033ecd989153441b9","source_text":"$a\\le a_1\\le b_1\\ldots\\le a_n\\le b_n\\le b$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt225.tex:351","target_normalized_sha256":"65552827ef94d5f41e068b86b5d85b7fedc1e7ce160e2d4b70777c00c198c86c","target_text":"$a\\le a_1\\le b_1\\le\\ldots\\le a_n\\le b_n\\le b$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S225"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-finite-union-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0059","math_ordinal":278,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The decomposition of F_m defines intervals [c_i,d_i] only for i through n, with n at most m; the image union must therefore run through n, not through the unrelated upper bound m.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt225.tex:379","source_normalized_sha256":"d21bfbc91b5f8e4b32c455f78f5bc282feab354b2907fb2618281f86bae08aa0","source_text":"$\\bigcup_{i\\le m}f[\\,[c_i,d_i],]$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt225.tex:376","target_normalized_sha256":"45f940bcb82d5661038d9d5ca1f7cac5f3522ee69be238ea8f554d0c941f4b21","target_text":"$\\bigcup_{i\\le n}f[\\,[c_i,d_i],]$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S225"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-set-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0060","math_ordinal":367,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Only E_n and G_n are defined in this construction; h_2 and the preceding set F also use G_n setminus E_n, so both occurrences of the undefined F_n must be E_n.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt225.tex:509-510","source_normalized_sha256":"e63643f77f19a75279829101cfff4d09c1dc1950a315af38e9e382ca45a44e27","source_text":"$\\mu_D(D\\cap G_n\\setminus F_n)$ and $\\mu(G_n\\setminus F_n)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt225.tex:506-507","target_normalized_sha256":"f2479e931bf79e59d29c5ed652ea898a5a39727bb66f5a0d8944794126b0a5e6","target_text":"$\\mu_D(D\\cap G_n\\setminus E_n)$ dan $\\mu(G_n\\setminus E_n)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S225"}
{"classification":"mathematical-duplicated-factor","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0061","math_ordinal":427,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The defining estimate contributes one factor 2^{-k}; the authority repeats it inside the limit but immediately concludes with a single factor, so removing the duplicate restores the stated bound.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt225.tex:611","source_normalized_sha256":"ff9df06c79f5085c7eca23098c9196666867ffc2299bde50ad8ac21499dd4c2c","source_text":"$\\le 2^{-k}\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}2^{-k}|y-x_n|$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt225.tex:608","target_normalized_sha256":"6f39f2655b09ffc6f29d77351a677a000725352958791044c27a56e118a4f04d","target_text":"$\\le 2^{-k}\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}|y-x_n|$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S225"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-approximated-function","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0062","math_ordinal":492,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The construction uses p_i to approximate f'(x), and the next sentence concludes f' is the limit of f_k; the bound must therefore compare f_k with f', not with f.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt225.tex:674","source_normalized_sha256":"d2c2491d9c2fe34f0b2c591fa852136c513b0b0e3a513f325b79c07d4a201943","source_text":"$|f(x)-f_k(x)|\\le 2^{-k}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt225.tex:675","target_normalized_sha256":"ba819d9740c116832359de7a0863ffe17f2e418e2dd2d407e71fd2f2a2d02856","target_text":"$|f'(x)-f_k(x)|\\le 2^{-k}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S225"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-punctured-neighborhood","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0063","math_ordinal":548,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The displayed difference quotient has denominator x-c and is undefined at x=c; adding the strict positive lower bound states the punctured neighborhood required by differentiability while leaving the preceding condition on g unchanged.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt225.tex:728","source_normalized_sha256":"f905b8052ccb55cf10cbfaac1c12637d6c20dd869f21db3c524773e746c9a316","source_text":"$|x-c|\\le\\delta$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt225.tex:729","target_normalized_sha256":"3b2311fceeffdab8f38a4d359b660a3d6095e2d01ae1227a09b932ef100ddc66","target_text":"$0<|x-c|\\le\\delta$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S225"}
